WEBVTT

00:25.741 --> 00:30.078
FOOL NIGHT

01:42.025 --> 01:42.859
TRANSFLORA MEDICAL

01:42.943 --> 01:44.653
We've had enough of this inhumane system!

01:44.736 --> 01:46.738
Reduce the Oxygen Tax!

01:52.202 --> 01:54.454
Hey! All we were doing was protesting!

01:54.955 --> 01:56.331
You're the ones who attacked us!

01:56.414 --> 01:58.667
You have no right
to keep us locked in here!

01:58.750 --> 02:00.752
- How much longer until you let us out?
- Let us out!

02:00.836 --> 02:02.504
If you want to get out it will cost you.

02:02.587 --> 02:04.464
Bail is 1.2 million yen.

02:04.548 --> 02:08.635
The fine is 400,000.
20,000 for damages to the riot police.

02:08.718 --> 02:10.011
You have no choice but to pay.

02:10.095 --> 02:11.429
You know that we can't pay that!

02:11.513 --> 02:13.390
We were protesting
because we don't have money!

02:13.473 --> 02:15.809
- So you want us to go to prison?
- Come on!

02:15.892 --> 02:17.477
I don't want to go to prison.

02:17.561 --> 02:19.187
I don't want to go to prison.

02:19.271 --> 02:21.439
I don't want to go to prison.

02:21.523 --> 02:24.192
Don't worry, you won't be going to prison.

02:24.985 --> 02:28.071
If you don't have any money,
then you'll go to Paupertown instead.

02:29.781 --> 02:31.116
We'd go to Paupertown?

02:31.241 --> 02:32.701
What the hell? I'm not doing that!

02:32.784 --> 02:35.078
You're going to strip us of everything
and throw us out?

02:35.162 --> 02:37.372
- There's no way we can survive!
- You can't send us there!

02:37.455 --> 02:39.749
- Now what? Now what?
- Come back here!

02:39.833 --> 02:41.168
Dad, what do we do?

02:41.251 --> 02:42.169
Dad!

02:42.252 --> 02:44.921
- Dad! Dad, I'm scared!
- You can't force us to go there!

03:34.721 --> 03:36.932
<i>This is where Ivy…</i>

03:39.142 --> 03:40.101
<i>I…</i>

03:45.148 --> 03:47.150
<i>What did I come here to do?</i>

04:38.285 --> 04:41.496
Paupertown is an old residential district

04:41.579 --> 04:44.582
where people who can no longer afford
to live in the city have ended up.

04:44.666 --> 04:46.501
It's essentially a big slum.

04:54.551 --> 04:58.221
It doesn't have an underground
heating system like the city does.

04:58.305 --> 05:01.975
So the snow that fell here 100 years
ago is still frozen.

05:02.058 --> 05:04.561
But… the air is fresh.

05:04.644 --> 05:05.562
Hmm.

05:11.818 --> 05:13.403
There aren't actually that many people

05:13.486 --> 05:15.572
who've undergone Transfloration
in the city.

05:15.655 --> 05:19.117
Most of the Spiriflora we have there
are brought in from Paupertown.

05:19.200 --> 05:20.660
They bring them into the city

05:20.744 --> 05:23.621
after they've undergone
Complete Transfloration.

05:23.705 --> 05:25.749
Isn't that extra work?

05:25.832 --> 05:27.125
It's for the city's appearance.

05:27.792 --> 05:29.753
People undergoing
Late Stage Transfloration

05:29.836 --> 05:32.047
are an unsettling reminder of death.

05:32.130 --> 05:34.507
If you saw them all the time,
you'd get depressed.

05:35.508 --> 05:36.968
Oh.

05:43.892 --> 05:46.061
Wha… Wha… What's going on?

05:46.144 --> 05:47.687
Are we gonna be okay?

05:48.396 --> 05:50.273
The Parade is going to start soon.

06:39.239 --> 06:42.575
There are about 15,000 people
living in Paupertown.

06:42.659 --> 06:45.453
The heat and food they need
to keep them from dying,

06:45.537 --> 06:49.416
those are both paid for
by Transfloration Subsidies.

06:49.499 --> 06:52.877
In Paupertown, Transfloration Subsidies
intended for one person

06:52.961 --> 06:56.256
are distributed to all households here
to cover living expenses.

06:56.339 --> 06:59.426
Each year, about 100 people
come to Transflora Medical

06:59.509 --> 07:01.511
to give up their lives for money.

07:02.470 --> 07:04.764
The Parade that
you wanted to come here to see?

07:07.225 --> 07:09.686
It's a shipment of sacrifices.

07:30.707 --> 07:33.126
It's the 24th century.
How is this allowed?

07:33.209 --> 07:35.003
That's just how it is.

07:35.086 --> 07:37.839
But why are children being chosen

07:37.922 --> 07:41.342
when there are so many adults
and elderly people?

07:41.426 --> 07:44.012
You did read the report
that I gave you, right?

07:44.721 --> 07:48.057
It's based on who can be used
in Human-Sourced Furniture.

07:48.141 --> 07:51.769
An older persons Spiriflor
doesn't produce that much wood.

07:52.729 --> 07:56.149
Whereas young children
turn into large Spiriflora.

07:56.858 --> 07:58.693
If they're raised properly and sold,

07:58.776 --> 08:01.321
they can be worth close to 10 million yen.

08:05.825 --> 08:08.244
Did Yomiko know about this?

08:10.413 --> 08:13.416
Did she know and still do that
to Ivy's sister?

08:20.215 --> 08:22.217
All employees know about it.

08:22.300 --> 08:24.093
It's something they were taught.

08:29.182 --> 08:34.062
Yesterday, you were burning for revenge,
but now you're at a loss?

08:34.145 --> 08:36.064
You can blame Yomiko all you want,

08:36.147 --> 08:38.316
but as long as you work
at Transflora Medical,

08:38.399 --> 08:40.610
you're just as guilty as she is.

08:42.153 --> 08:43.404
And I am as well.

08:47.784 --> 08:50.286
Hold on, you said
"Ivy's sister", didn't you?

08:52.455 --> 08:54.707
So you really did talk to Ivy.

08:55.625 --> 08:58.753
Tell me what happened
and what it is you're able to do.

08:59.879 --> 09:02.173
If it's true that Ivy was born
in Paupertown,

09:02.257 --> 09:04.425
then I think we could find some clues
while we're here.

09:04.926 --> 09:07.303
Whatever we find
could bring us one step closer

09:07.387 --> 09:09.722
to answering the questions
surrounding Ivy.

09:14.435 --> 09:17.689
If we figure out the truth,
we can tell the protesters.

09:17.772 --> 09:20.275
I can't force you to answer, but…

09:22.485 --> 09:23.903
Tell me now, idiot!

09:26.197 --> 09:27.031
Yeah, okay.

09:27.115 --> 09:30.118
I'm gonna go over there.

09:30.201 --> 09:31.369
Thank you.

09:31.452 --> 09:32.912
No biggie.

09:32.996 --> 09:35.748
There are some things
that are just better left unknown.

09:35.832 --> 09:37.792
Keep your voices down, 'kay?

09:39.794 --> 09:41.129
All right.

09:45.717 --> 09:48.052
I underwent Transfloration
three months ago.

09:48.636 --> 09:51.723
It gave me the ability
to hear the voices of Spiriflora.

09:55.727 --> 09:58.938
Okay boys, I want you to stay close to me.
Got it?

10:02.650 --> 10:04.110
Where are we going?

10:04.193 --> 10:07.071
I wanted to meet the boss of Paupertown.

10:07.155 --> 10:11.242
He could help us find the Plantation Owner
who knows about Shiika Izumi.

10:11.326 --> 10:13.494
P… Plantation?

10:22.837 --> 10:24.422
Sorry to interrupt you all.

10:24.505 --> 10:27.300
I wanted to ask you something
about Human-Sourced Furniture.

10:28.676 --> 10:30.136
Where'd you come from?

10:30.553 --> 10:32.055
Transflora Medical.

10:33.348 --> 10:34.724
Don't worry.

10:34.807 --> 10:36.517
We're not here to bust you.

10:39.896 --> 10:41.147
So what do you want?

10:41.230 --> 10:44.275
I wanted to make a deal
with the Plantation Owner.

10:44.359 --> 10:46.861
The cabriole-legged wardrobe
I just bought,

10:46.944 --> 10:48.696
it's a beautiful piece of work.

10:48.780 --> 10:51.032
It was all made from
a single piece of wood.

10:51.115 --> 10:52.867
I adore the grain on it.

10:53.451 --> 10:57.538
I heard that it was made from a Spiriflor
grown at a Plantation near here.

10:57.622 --> 11:00.458
I was hoping to place an order
for another piece.

11:01.626 --> 11:04.045
Would you introduce me to the owner?

11:08.800 --> 11:10.635
This is the Plantation up ahead.

11:11.427 --> 11:13.596
You might want to look down
while we walk through here.

11:13.680 --> 11:14.847
Hmm.

11:38.079 --> 11:40.415
I think I'm gonna puke.

11:41.332 --> 11:43.626
Once the children
who are selected for the Parade

11:43.710 --> 11:46.295
reach a certain stage of Transfloration,

11:46.379 --> 11:48.464
they're sent to the Plantation,

11:48.548 --> 11:51.509
where they're carefully cultivated
into high quality wood.

11:54.387 --> 11:57.348
Those stumps are the remains
of the harvested ones.

11:57.432 --> 11:59.225
They also serve as gravestones.

12:02.061 --> 12:05.106
Hey. That's the Plantation Owner's house.

12:14.907 --> 12:16.909
<i>Everything in here's made of wood.</i>

12:16.993 --> 12:18.077
Pleasure to meet you.

12:18.786 --> 12:21.289
I bought furniture made from
a Spiriflor grown here.

12:21.372 --> 12:23.040
I was very impressed with it.

12:23.124 --> 12:25.168
It made me want to reserve another one.

12:25.251 --> 12:27.712
So I came to your Plantation
to see if I could.

12:42.018 --> 12:43.728
Write your name down.

12:43.811 --> 12:45.354
The wait is two years.

12:51.611 --> 12:53.404
I was at a friend's house before,

12:53.488 --> 12:56.449
and we were showing each other
our furniture collections.

12:56.532 --> 12:59.243
One piece they had
really caught my eye though, you know.

12:59.327 --> 13:02.830
Apparently, it was made from
a girl named Shiika Izumi?

13:03.372 --> 13:04.707
I was interested in finding out

13:04.791 --> 13:08.336
what her life was like
before her Transfloration.

13:08.419 --> 13:10.671
Do you happen to know anything about her?

13:13.966 --> 13:17.345
It's on page 156
of that notebook you have.

13:17.428 --> 13:18.679
SHIIKA IZUMI

13:26.521 --> 13:27.939
Thank you.

13:31.651 --> 13:32.985
SHIIKA

13:33.069 --> 13:34.737
Ivy put that there.

13:36.364 --> 13:37.782
This place is awful.

13:39.325 --> 13:42.662
Hey, isn't there anything we can do
to save these children?

13:42.745 --> 13:44.372
You have connections!

13:44.455 --> 13:45.540
So what you mean is,

13:45.623 --> 13:49.085
you want to bust all
the Human-Sourced Furniture businesses,

13:49.168 --> 13:51.504
and cut off the income
for the people of Paupertown?

13:52.129 --> 13:54.090
You want to let them starve to death?

14:00.012 --> 14:01.430
This is so cruel.

14:07.854 --> 14:09.814
Listen, I'm going to tell you something.

14:09.897 --> 14:12.275
The Transfloration System is no different

14:12.358 --> 14:14.902
except for the fact that
it's on a much larger scale.

14:14.986 --> 14:16.654
It's what's known as the trolley problem.

14:17.655 --> 14:20.783
<i>We use money to lure people</i>
<i>into undergoing Transfloration,</i>

14:20.867 --> 14:24.537
<i>sacrificing a few so that countless others</i>
<i>can get oxygen to breathe.</i>

14:24.620 --> 14:25.621
<i>It's all the same.</i>

14:25.705 --> 14:27.290
<i>The only difference with Transfloration</i>

14:27.373 --> 14:29.542
<i>is that what you get out of it</i>
<i>is invisible.</i>

14:30.167 --> 14:33.045
That's what it means to be involved
with Transfloration.

14:34.714 --> 14:37.550
The work you're doing
is helping improve the lives of others.

14:37.633 --> 14:39.886
It's for a cause bigger than yourself.

14:39.969 --> 14:43.472
You were lucky enough
to not be born in a place like this.

14:45.474 --> 14:47.143
Work hard. Make money.

14:47.226 --> 14:49.020
Keep improving.

14:49.103 --> 14:51.439
Otherwise,
you are going to wind up right here.

14:52.023 --> 14:56.944
DROP DEAD

15:06.996 --> 15:08.456
SHIIKA IZUMI12-20 BLDG. B 603

15:39.487 --> 15:41.989
What's wrong? Hey, you good?

15:43.532 --> 15:44.992
Yeah, I'm fine.

15:45.076 --> 15:47.995
I was feeling a little bit dizzy is all.

15:49.580 --> 15:52.583
Just close your eyes
and face the direction of the light.

15:55.419 --> 15:56.712
Is that helping?

15:56.796 --> 15:59.507
Doesn't it feel like
you're standing in a bright room?

16:06.013 --> 16:07.098
Thank you.

16:15.064 --> 16:17.316
MUKURU & SHIIKA IZUMI

16:17.900 --> 16:19.318
<i>"Mukuru Izumi."</i>

16:20.111 --> 16:21.779
<i>So that's Ivy's real name.</i>

16:47.430 --> 16:50.057
This is where Ivy…

17:00.026 --> 17:01.027
Hmm.

17:07.366 --> 17:11.120
O… Sa… Saken.

17:11.662 --> 17:13.581
- Is that a… Huh?
- So what's happenin'?

17:13.664 --> 17:15.624
You pickin' up on somethin' here?

17:15.708 --> 17:17.543
Okay, wait, don't tell me. I wanna guess.

17:17.626 --> 17:18.753
You're a psychic.

17:18.836 --> 17:20.463
Mm. Well, yeah, I mean it's…

17:20.546 --> 17:22.256
It's basically like that.

17:22.339 --> 17:24.884
Cool. Well, take your time.

17:29.138 --> 17:30.389
How cute.

17:31.182 --> 17:33.017
They're candy wrappers.

17:33.642 --> 17:37.063
There were reports that
Ivy was stealing candy from his victims.

17:40.483 --> 17:42.818
All of these ones are pretty old, though.

17:42.902 --> 17:46.113
I'm assuming Ivy or Shiika Izumi
dug through the trash

17:46.197 --> 17:48.324
and kept all the candy wrappers
they found.

17:54.080 --> 17:55.623
That's blood.

17:56.624 --> 17:58.751
We should take this sheet back with us.

18:02.838 --> 18:03.839
Huh?

18:05.925 --> 18:08.052
That's a petal from a camellia.

18:08.135 --> 18:09.303
It's all dried up though.

18:10.346 --> 18:13.474
I thought Ivy was an Uncaria rhynchopylla.

18:13.557 --> 18:16.102
Well, maybe someone
who turned into a camellia

18:16.185 --> 18:18.896
moved in here after everyone else left.

18:23.442 --> 18:24.527
Anything?

18:25.361 --> 18:26.195
Just be quiet.

18:26.278 --> 18:27.571
HIKA, OTSA, SAKEN, KUDAI, RO

18:27.655 --> 18:30.032
They… They're both saying something.

18:30.116 --> 18:32.368
The song they sang at the Parade.

18:33.452 --> 18:34.620
Okay, let me see.

18:34.703 --> 18:38.833
"Hika, Otsa, Saken." "Kudai, Ro…"

18:38.916 --> 18:40.209
What's that word?

18:40.292 --> 18:42.044
"Ota…"

18:42.753 --> 18:43.712
Otaro Kudai?

18:44.839 --> 18:48.050
Then the other one must be… Ken Hikasa?

18:48.134 --> 18:49.426
Who are they?

18:49.510 --> 18:50.553
Do you know them?

18:51.178 --> 18:52.721
Otaro Kudai is…

18:52.805 --> 18:56.142
He's one of the three researchers
who first invented Transfloration.

18:56.225 --> 18:59.562
Ken Hikasa is a leader
of the Anti-Transfloration Movement.

19:00.312 --> 19:03.649
If both of their names are being
spoken in this room, then…

19:09.947 --> 19:11.699
They made him.

19:11.782 --> 19:13.200
They made Ivy in this room.

19:13.284 --> 19:17.454
The Anti-Transfloration Movement got help
from one of the top scientists.

19:17.955 --> 19:20.875
I get it now. I never thought they would…

19:20.958 --> 19:24.128
We've underestimated
the Anti-Transfloration Movement.

19:24.628 --> 19:26.505
Huh? Wait a minute.

19:26.589 --> 19:28.507
Why would they make someone
do the thing they're against?

19:29.800 --> 19:31.760
I don't think making Ivy
was ever their goal.

19:32.511 --> 19:34.388
Getting Ivy to commit mass murders

19:34.471 --> 19:37.266
and the widespread protests against them…

19:37.349 --> 19:38.893
That was their goal.

19:39.518 --> 19:42.938
They want the public to despise
the Transfloration system.

19:43.022 --> 19:46.442
They think if that happens,
then they can abolish the whole thing.

19:47.276 --> 19:49.278
That's what they're really after.

19:50.946 --> 19:53.741
And I went and pulled
the trigger for them.

20:01.999 --> 20:03.375
<i>He's furious.</i>

20:04.668 --> 20:06.420
I get it now.

20:06.503 --> 20:10.216
Why they didn't make it public when
Ivy killed one of the Movement's leaders.

20:10.299 --> 20:12.343
They wanted to wait
till things got this bad

20:12.426 --> 20:14.303
to release the information.

20:14.386 --> 20:16.180
Even though Ivy can't talk,

20:16.263 --> 20:19.099
he was able to steal the desk
from the Hiyama's hidden room,

20:19.183 --> 20:20.935
because he had an accomplice.

20:22.353 --> 20:24.146
Ah, shit!

20:24.230 --> 20:25.356
I feel so stupid!

20:27.608 --> 20:28.901
Well, do you know where…

20:28.984 --> 20:30.236
Where those two men are?

20:30.861 --> 20:33.822
Dr. Kudai's been missing
for a pretty long time now.

20:33.906 --> 20:35.699
A lot of people think he's dead.

20:36.408 --> 20:39.995
However, we should be able to get
into contact with Ken Hikasa.

20:40.955 --> 20:42.164
That's what we'll do.

20:43.332 --> 20:45.376
Let's go find Ken Hikasa.

20:50.965 --> 20:53.217
I'd say coming here was worth it.

20:53.300 --> 20:54.635
I'm glad that we did.

20:54.718 --> 20:55.886
Yeah.

20:55.970 --> 20:57.012
If we can get proof that

20:57.096 --> 20:59.473
the Anti-Tranfloration Movement
created Ivy,

20:59.556 --> 21:01.558
we can protect Transflora Medical.
